Monks, if a lay devotee's house is endowed with these nine factors, one should not visit if one has not yet gone, and if one has already gone, one should not sit down.

Monks, if a lay devotee's house is endowed with these nine factors, it is proper to visit if one has not yet gone, and if one has already gone, it is proper to sit down. What are the nine? They are:
(1) Welcoming with affection upon arrival;
(2) Paying homage with affection;
(3) Offering a seat with affection;
(4) Not hiding existing offerings from the monks;
(5) Giving much when there are many offerings available;
(6) Giving excellent offerings when excellent offerings are available;
(7) Giving respectfully, not disrespectfully;
(8) Approaching and sitting near a monk to listen to the Dhamma;
(9) Listening respectfully to the Dhamma preached by that monk.

